{"base_rate":0.2638700947225981,"brier":0.12418646820027063,"bss":0.3606632899698341,"bss_hi":0.4388551311443974,"bss_lo":0.27488184129108256,"chart":{"base":[404.2,136.5],"fp":[252.0,302.7],"lead":"62,254.7 272,229.7 482,191 692,114.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.36 — higher than 63% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +10pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 63% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 6%; promised 86% → rained 77%"},"rel":"65.8,439.2 234,327.1 604.6,135.5"},"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.06235453315290937,"ess":352.3934282992957,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Zaragoza</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Zaragoza rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>79%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 739 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nZARAGOZA AEROPUERTO, 10.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.36, ranked 50 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(29&ndash;82) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>350</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>95</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Zaragoza</b> <span class=\"muted\">ES</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>29&ndash;82\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>739 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Zaragoza &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Zaragoza\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.08260869565217,350.3478260869565 109.38589473684212,305.36842105263156 211.24473684210523,185.6315789473684 322.4067647058824,71.52941176470591 396.8348148148149,18.0 396.8348148148149,49.45679012345681 322.4067647058824,146.47058823529412 211.24473684210523,262.2631578947368 109.38589473684212,351.34736842105264 71.08260869565217,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"285.9512855209743\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"285.9512855209743\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,362.24 71.08260869565217,345.07246376811594 109.38589473684212,297.7052631578947 211.24473684210523,223.94736842105263 322.4067647058824,114.35294117647055 396.8348148148149,94.39506172839509\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 350 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"362.24\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"71.08260869565217\" cy=\"345.07246376811594\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 95 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"109.38589473684212\" cy=\"297.7052631578947\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 43%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"211.24473684210523\" cy=\"223.94736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"322.4067647058824\" cy=\"114.35294117647055\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.8348148148149\" cy=\"94.39506172839509\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(26%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Zaragoza the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.43) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.207</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.335</td><td class='num'>9.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'>0.405</td><td class='num'>3.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>209</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.427</td><td class='num'>6.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":41.65606,"lon":-0.87734,"n":739,"n_cities":134,"name":"Zaragoza","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":350,"obs":0.054285714285714284,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03695652173913042,"n":69,"obs":0.10144927536231885,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.14515789473684212,"n":95,"obs":0.23157894736842105,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6,"lo"